{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:BraidsAndKnots.ThreeStrandColorWindingRigidity","@type":"LeanModule","name":"BraidsAndKnots.ThreeStrandColorWindingRigidity","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:Mathlib.Tactic"],"declarations":20,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidsAndKnots.axial_eq_div","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidsAndKnots.axial_eq_div","kind":"theorem","line":198,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/braids-and-knots/three-strand-color-winding-rigidity.lean#L198-L205","doc":"Over a field with `1 - q⁴ ≠ 0`, the relation `a · (1 − q⁴) = h`\nused above is literally the classical Hoefsmit quotient\n`a₂ = h / (1 − q⁴)`. Nothing is lost by carrying the relation. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidsAndKnots.threeStrand_cubes_to_one","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidsAndKnots.threeStrand_cubes_to_one","kind":"theorem","line":172,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/braids-and-knots/three-strand-color-winding-rigidity.lean#L172-L184","doc":"**Rigidity of the color winding (the cube identity).** The uniform\nthree-strand rotation on the (2,1) block cubes to the identity for\nevery `q` with `1 - q²` invertible — exactly and q-independently:\nthe ζ₃ color winding of the (3,k) torus tower is topological. ","formalizes":[{"@id":"block:prop:three-strand-color-winding-rigidity","label":"prop:three-strand-color-winding-rigidity","md":"quantum-observable-universe/braids-and-knots/three-strand-color-winding-rigidity.md"}],"signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidsAndKnots.threeStrand_det","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidsAndKnots.threeStrand_det","kind":"theorem","line":161,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/braids-and-knots/three-strand-color-winding-rigidity.lean#L161-L170","doc":"**Determinant is `1`** — exactly the Hoefsmit constraint on β.\nNeeds no invertibility hypothesis at all: it is an identity in\n`ℤ[q, q⁻¹][a, β]` modulo the amplitude's defining quadratic. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidsAndKnots.threeStrand_trace","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidsAndKnots.threeStrand_trace","kind":"theorem","line":144,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/braids-and-knots/three-strand-color-winding-rigidity.lean#L144-L159","doc":"**Trace is `-1`, q-independently** (no β involved).\n\nThe only hypothesis is that `1 - q²` is invertible. It is genuine\nrather than technical: at `q² = 1` the Hoefsmit defining relation\n`a · (1 - q⁴) = h` degenerates to `0 = 0` and constrains `a` not at\nall, so the trace really is unconstrained there. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidsAndKnots.threeStrandRotation_eq_product","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidsAndKnots.threeStrandRotation_eq_product","kind":"theorem","line":132,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/braids-and-knots/three-strand-color-winding-rigidity.lean#L132-L138","doc":"The rotation is honestly the product `σ₁ · σ₂` of the diagonal lepton\nchannel matrix and the symmetric Hoefsmit block. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidsAndKnots.threeStrandRotation","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidsAndKnots.threeStrandRotation","kind":"def","line":123,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/braids-and-knots/three-strand-color-winding-rigidity.lean#L123-L130","doc":"The (2,1) Hoefsmit block of the uniform three-strand rotation\n`σ₁σ₂`: `σ₁ = diag(q, -q⁻¹)` times the axial-distance-2 Hoefsmit\nblock for `σ₂` with axial entry `a` and binding amplitude `β`.\nEntries written out (the product of the diagonal and the symmetric\nblock). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidsAndKnots.axialNeg_rel","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidsAndKnots.axialNeg_rel","kind":"theorem","line":112,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/braids-and-knots/three-strand-color-winding-rigidity.lean#L112-L121","doc":"The derived entry satisfies its own Hoefsmit defining relation\n`a₋₂ · (1 − q⁻⁴) = h`, given only `a₂ · (1 − q⁴) = h`. No\ninvertibility, no division. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidsAndKnots.axialNeg","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidsAndKnots.axialNeg","kind":"def","line":107,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/braids-and-knots/three-strand-color-winding-rigidity.lean#L107-L110","doc":"The Hoefsmit axial-distance `−2` entry, derived from the `+2` entry:\n`a₋₂ = −q⁴ · a₂`. (Over a field this is\n`h/(1 − q⁻⁴) = −q⁴ · h/(1 − q⁴)`.) ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidsAndKnots.heckeH","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidsAndKnots.heckeH","kind":"def","line":104,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/braids-and-knots/three-strand-color-winding-rigidity.lean#L104-L105","doc":"Hecke amplitude `h = q − q⁻¹`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidsAndKnots.M2.cube_of_trace_det","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidsAndKnots.M2.cube_of_trace_det","kind":"theorem","line":94,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/braids-and-knots/three-strand-color-winding-rigidity.lean#L94-L98","doc":"ζ₃ rigidity, packaged: trace `-1` and determinant `1` force `M³ = 1`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidsAndKnots.M2.cube_of_quadratic","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidsAndKnots.M2.cube_of_quadratic","kind":"theorem","line":79,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/braids-and-knots/three-strand-color-winding-rigidity.lean#L79-L92","doc":"**Cayley–Hamilton, ζ₃ case (cube).** A 2×2 matrix satisfying the ζ₃\nquadratic cubes to the identity. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidsAndKnots.M2.quadratic_of_trace_det","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidsAndKnots.M2.quadratic_of_trace_det","kind":"theorem","line":67,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/braids-and-knots/three-strand-color-winding-rigidity.lean#L67-L77","doc":"**Cayley–Hamilton, ζ₃ case (quadratic).** A 2×2 matrix with trace\n`-1` and determinant `1` satisfies `M² = -M - 1` entrywise. Pure\ncommutative-ring algebra. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidsAndKnots.M2.one","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidsAndKnots.M2.one","kind":"def","line":64,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/braids-and-knots/three-strand-color-winding-rigidity.lean#L64-L65","doc":"Identity. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidsAndKnots.M2.mul","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidsAndKnots.M2.mul","kind":"def","line":59,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/braids-and-knots/three-strand-color-winding-rigidity.lean#L59-L62","doc":"2×2 matrix product. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidsAndKnots.M2.d","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidsAndKnots.M2.d","kind":"def","line":53,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/braids-and-knots/three-strand-color-winding-rigidity.lean#L53-L53","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidsAndKnots.M2.c","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidsAndKnots.M2.c","kind":"def","line":52,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/braids-and-knots/three-strand-color-winding-rigidity.lean#L52-L52","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidsAndKnots.M2.b","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidsAndKnots.M2.b","kind":"def","line":51,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/braids-and-knots/three-strand-color-winding-rigidity.lean#L51-L51","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidsAndKnots.M2.a","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidsAndKnots.M2.a","kind":"def","line":50,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/braids-and-knots/three-strand-color-winding-rigidity.lean#L50-L50","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidsAndKnots.M2.mk","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidsAndKnots.M2.mk","kind":"ctor","line":49,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/braids-and-knots/three-strand-color-winding-rigidity.lean#L49-L49","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidsAndKnots.M2","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidsAndKnots.M2","kind":"structure","line":48,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/braids-and-knots/three-strand-color-winding-rigidity.lean#L48-L53","doc":"Minimal 2×2 matrix carrier (row-major entries). ","signatureChunk":0}]}